About Grupo QuintoAndar

We are Grupo QuintoAndar, the largest real estate ecosystem in Latin America. Guided by a shared purpose of helping people love where they live, we have a diversified portfolio of brands and solutions across different countries in Latin America, covering all phases of the housing journey. We also have a Technology Hub in Portugal. We develop technology and innovation to transform and enhance the overall living experience.

With the support of a world-class team of investors and advisors, including Kaszek, Qualcomm, General Atlantic, and SoftBank, Grupo QuintoAndar is currently valued at over USD 5.1 billion and continues to grow year over year.

Here, you will work with top professionals in the market, in an environment that breathes innovation, collaboration, and high performance. To learn more about our story, visit: https://grupoquintoandar.com/pt/ .

&nbsp;

Why is this position affirmatively focused on people with disabilities?

Grupo QuintoAndar is committed to promoting Social Inclusion, and one of our key pillars is representation within our teams. By creating more opportunities and taking intentional action, we can advance the development and strengthening of social inclusion in our workplace.
It is essential to note that our hiring process for this position remains unchanged in terms of stages and evaluation methods. We understand that recruitment is a gateway to diversity, and we are always attentive to what makes us plural.

&nbsp;

Location &amp; Hybrid Work Model for hybrid positions

Our team follows a “hybrid” model, requiring in-person attendance at our office located in São Paulo.

&nbsp;

Hiring Process Stages

The stages of our hiring processes aim to assess your experiences and allow you to meet our teams and explore career opportunities. They are structured as follows:

• Submitting your application;

• Validation of a disability medical report;

• People Interview;

• Hiring Manager Interview;

• Case;

• Stakeholder Interview;

• Offer!

About the Team

QuintoAndar is seeking a hands-on, highly organized, and detail-oriented Fintech Regulatory Specialist to join our Legal &amp; Regulatory team. As we verticalize our financial stack and secure our institutional autonomy, this role will serve as the strategic technical architect and expert for our regulatory compliance infrastructure. Working with technical full autonomy, you will design scalable compliance systems, serve as an internal advisor across the Legal Org and senior leadership, and leverage modern AI and automation tools to drive high-speed regulatory execution.&nbsp;

Key Responsibilities

• Regulatory Project Management: Design, implement, and maintain robust, audit-proof compliance frameworks across Central Bank (BCB) licensing pipelines (SCFI and Consórcio). Build scalable processes that enable peer execution while mentoring less experienced lawyers on the team.&nbsp;

• Reporting &amp; Data Infrastructure: Reporting Strategy &amp; Automation: Architect, automate, and oversee data infrastructure for mandatory BCB reporting (STA, Unicad, Sisorf, Document 2080), ensuring long-term systemic reliability and data integrity while overseeing operational execution.&nbsp;

• Cross-Functional Alignment: Functional Alignment: Serve as the primary regulatory advisor for Product, Tech, Finance (COSIF), and Compliance. Evaluate complex, multi-variable legal scenarios to create scalable regulatory strategies that unlock business opportunities while mitigating institutional risk.&nbsp;

• Routine Inquiries &amp; Research: Leverage AI and modern tech tools to deliver rapid, high-impact synthesis on evolving BCB frameworks (e.g., CP 108/BaaS). Act as QuintoAndar's primary representative in key industry forums, contributing directly to public consultations and market policy discussions.&nbsp;

Qualifications &amp; Requirements

• Education: Law degree with 8+ years with post-graduation experience and active OAB registration. A Postgrad

