ABOUT US

Capco is a global technology and management consultancy specializing in driving digital transformation in the financial services and insurance industries. Capco is committed to providing clients with practical solutions. We offer a globally integrated service with offices in leading financial centers across the globe. We have the people, the vision, and the passion.

We are growing through a significant growth journey, now is a very good time to join us as we expand geographically, increase headcount and disrupt the consulting market across APAC with entrepreneurial and agile thinking.

We are:

• Experts in banking and payments, capital markets and wealth and asset management

• Deep knowledge in financial services offering, including e.g. Finance, Risk and Compliance, Financial Crime, Core Banking etc.

• Committed to growing our business and hiring the best talent to help us get there

• Focus on maintaining our nimble, agile and entrepreneurial culture

&nbsp;

ROLE RESPONSIBILITIES

We are currently seeking multiple consultants and senior consultants to support and drive the growth of our Data practice, particularly in our Data governance and data management stream. This is an exciting opportunity to be a leader, in a growing team of data practitioners, where you will be initiating and implementing cutting-edge data &amp; analytics programmes for top-tier Financial Services clients.

This project is with a leading bank as a Business Analyst / Project Manager for Data governance and management project&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

KEY RESPONSIBILITIES&nbsp;

• Implement and maintain data governance frameworks, policies, standards, and best practices across the organization.

• Assisting to drive data quality initiatives, including defining controls, monitoring KPIs, and coordinating issue remediation.

• Support data ownership, stewardship, metadata management, and data lineage processes.

• Partner with business, technology, risk, and compliance stakeholders to ensure effective governance and regulatory compliance.

• Facilitate governance forums, stakeholder engagement, and training to promote data governance adoption.

• Support audit, regulatory, and enterprise data transformation initiatives through strong data management practices.

SKILLS &amp; EXPERTISE

• 3+ years of experience in Data Governance, Data Management , or data quality within financial services&nbsp;

• Good understanding of data governance, data quality, metadata management, and data lineage concepts.

• Experience on supporting and defining data strategies, target-state operating models , data capabilities, and implementation roadmaps to support business transformation and data-driven decision-making.

• Familiarity with data enablement process and delivered different strategies for refinement and improvement&nbsp;&nbsp;

• Excellent stakeholder management, communication, problem-solving, and analytical skills.

• Experience within Banking, Financial Services, Consulting, or other highly regulated environments is preferred

• SQL and relevant data governance certifications are advantageous.

ELIGIBILITY TO WORK IN SG

Applicants must have unrestricted working rights in Singapore. Only Singapore Citizens and Singapore Permanent Residents (PRs) will be considered. Employment Pass sponsorship is not available for this role.

&nbsp;

WHY CAPCO?  &nbsp;

We are expanding our business rapidly across Singapore and Asia. You will work on engaging projects with some of the largest banking and insurance clients in the world, projects that will deliver significant transformation and change.

&nbsp;

We are looking for a business-minded Sales Development Representative to initiate meetings for our Account Executives. This position will educate prospective clients on our company, culture, and products to grow business and schedule meetings for our Account Executive Team.
How our Sales Development Representatives spend their time:

• Make approximately 50 outbound calls per day to set appointments for our Account Executives for pre-employment services;

• Conduct approximately 50 communication outreach touchpoints via social media and email per day to build rapport for future sales;

• Set 25 appointments per month for the Account Executives;

• Initiate communication through outreach via email, LinkedIn, and phone calls to build rapport for future sales;

• Research prospective clients and pre-call planning;

• Manage pipeline through CRM Salesforce;

• Responsible for educating and developing prospects, leading to hand-off to the Account Executive team;

• Drive attendance for webinars and live seminars, set meetings for conferences;

• Collaborate with sales and marketing team members on a strategic sales approach;

• Ensure successful follow-through of the sales cycle by maintaining accurate activity and lead qualification information in the CRM application;

• Perform other duties as assigned.

What you bring:

• Ability to maintain regular and punctual attendance;

• Encourage a direct and positive relationship between the community and the company;

• Able to thrive in a fast-paced environment;

• You are a natural problem solver and are focused on creating solutions;

• You can adapt quickly to a changing environment;

• You work well independently but understand the importance of teamwork;

• Strong verbal and written communication skills, including the ability to effectively facilitate and adjust communication styles to the audience.

Requirements

• B2B Sales experience

• At least 2 years of experience in coldcalling / lead generation for IT staffing and professional services

• High School Diploma or equivalent required;

• Working knowledge of G-Suite and Microsoft Office Applications;

• Experience using Salesforce or similar CRM;

• Experience working in a call center environment focused on cold calling and closing sales preferred;

• Experience as a Sales Development Representative for other companies that deliver human resource software solutions preferred.

Minimum Technical and Work Environment Requirements:

• Internet Connection:

• Primary internet connection with a minimum speed of 15 Mbps .

• Backup internet connection with at least 10 Mbps .

• Backup connection must be capable of supporting work during a power outage.

• Primary Device:

• Desktop or laptop equipped with at least:

•
Intel Core i5 (8th generation or newer) , Intel Core i3 (10th generation or newer) , AMD Ryzen 5 , or an equivalent processor.

• A minimum of 8 GB RAM .

• Backup Device:

• Must meet or exceed the performance of an Intel Core i3 processor.

• Must be functional during power interruptions.

• Peripherals and Workspace:

• A functioning webcam .

• A noise-canceling USB headset .

• A quiet, dedicated home office space .

• A smartphone for communication and verification purposes.

Benefits

•
Join Our Dynamic Team: Experience our fun, inclusive, innovative culture that values your unique contributions and supports your professional growth.

•
Embrace the Opportunities: Seize daily chances to learn, innovate, and excel. Make a real impact in your field.

•
Limitless Career Growth: Unlock a world of possibilities and resources to propel your career forward.

•
Fast-Paced Thrills: Thrive in a high-energy, engaging atmosphere. Embrace challenges and reap stimulating rewards.

•
Flexibility, Your Way: Embrace the freedom to work from home or any location of your choice. Create your ideal work environment.

•
Work-Life Balance at Its Best: Say goodbye to stressful commutes and hello to quality time with loved ones. Achieve

At Flix, we offer a dynamic work environment with competitive pay, strong growth opportunities, and a tech-driven approach to making travel more accessible, sustainable, and affordable. &nbsp;

We're building one of India's most interesting marketing teams in the mobility space, and we need someone who can own a portfolio of channels the way a brand manager owns a category: with commercial instinct, cross-functional pull, and a genuine drive to grow.

This isn't a coordination role -you will own Brand partnerships, offline distribution, and OTA set strategy, run execution, and be accountable for outcomes. You'll work directly with the India Leadership and also operate as a key node between local teams and global stakeholders.

If you've grown up in FMCG or a fast-scaling startup and know what it means to own a channel from the ground up, this is the job.

About the Role

• You think about the Flix brand in India with both a short and long term lens. Contributing to how the brand shows up across your channels today while helping shape the positioning and perception we want to build over the next 3 to 5 years

• Build and manage Flix's B2B and brand partnership pipeline in India. Identifying prospects, closing deals, onboarding partners, and tracking commercial contribution to load

• Be the external face of Flix on OTA platforms, owning platform relationships, content quality, listing health, and commercial terms across all major OTA partners in India

• Manage the offline sales network. Travel agencies, ticket shops, and kiosks - from acquisition through to partner enablement, training, and performance management

• You collaborate across marketing, performance, CRM, and product to prevent channel strategies from running in silos and to unlock shared growth levers

• Identify and pursue new distribution and partnership opportunities in the Indian market, bringing commercial rigour to everything from a first pitch to a signed deal

• You liaise with HQ and global teams to keep local channel strategies aligned with Flix's broader commercial and brand direction

• You act as the primary external point of contact for partners across B2B, offline, and OTA, representing Flix with authority

About You

• 3 to 5 years in brand management, category management, or channel marketing, ideally in D2C, or a high-growth startup

• You've owned marketing spends or a channel target before, not just reported into one.&nbsp;

• Comfortable managing a wide portfolio without losing depth on what matters most.

• Strong negotiator and relationship builder. You can hold a room with a internal teams, external partner and on ground sales agents in the same day.&nbsp;

• Sharp with numbers, fast with decisions, and honest about what's working

We recognize that everyone carries a unique set of valuable skills and experiences. If you think you could have an impact even though you don't meet 100% of the requirements, we still encourage you to apply. We want to hear from you! &nbsp;

What We Offer

• Travel perks : 12 free Flix vouchers + 12 discount vouchers for friends &amp; family.&nbsp;

• Work from (M)Anywhere : Depending on your role, work from another location for up to 60 days per year.&nbsp;

• Hybrid work model : We are an office-first company, but we offer flexibility to balance work and life.&nbsp;

• Wellbeing support : Access confidential 1:1 counselling, courses, and stress management for yourself and up to four family members.&nbsp;

• Learning &amp; Development : Take advantage of language classes, training courses, and expert-led sessions to grow your skills.&nbsp;

• Mentoring Program : Connect with experienced colleagues to gain insights and accelerate your career.&nbsp;

